spindly creepy unsettling  skittering these are some of the words  and feelings that come to mind when you  think about the eight-legged arachnids  that plague  many of our nightmares it is no wonder  that spiders are used in many forms of  media  as elements of horror bent on  introducing fear into our hearts  video games are no exception especially  when it comes to the legend of zelda  one of the most recognizable monsters  plaguing the land of hyrule  is the unholy combination of a spider  with a human skull as its abdomen  called the sculptula the giant bone  spider looms above the ground  hanging from the branches of the trees  or a ceiling for hours on end  waiting silently for its prey to  unknowingly walk underneath its death  trap  and when the prey is in position it  swiftly and accurately swoops down to  entangle its next meal in a matter of  seconds with the sheer size of the  sculpture ranging from  1 to over 5 feet in diameter one finds  themselves  very thankful that they only exist  inside a video game  as they are absolutely large enough to  consume an unwitting human being that  just so happened to walk under the wrong  branch  the game that introduced these horrific  arachnids to the world was none other  than ocarina of time  which is a legendary zelda title well  known by fans for its darker undertones  see what i mean in the village of  kakariko which at one point was  inhabited solely by the mysterious chica  tribe  there stands a house that has long since  been abandoned  by its inhabitants or so the villagers  would like to believe  you see what crawls along the floors and  walls of that lonely house is neither  man nor  beast but the cursed family of  half-human half-sculptural amalgamations  for those familiar with the game you'll  recall that this family  is the reason that the gold sculptural  enemies exist their curse is somehow  bound to the existence of this  subspecies of sculptura  once all 100 of these golden spiders  have been killed throughout the land of  hyrule  and their tokens have been retrieved the  family's curse can be broken  but over the past two decades even  though there have been  countless theories covering why or how  the sculpture family became  cursed to begin with one that has seldom  been mentioned is who  exactly cursed them in this year's  halloween special  which you're currently watching i'm  going to cover all of it  so turn out your lights pay no attention  to the figure standing behind you  and follow me into the house of the  sculpture  as far as the family's origin is  concerned there are some who believe  that they are in fact  members of the sheikah clan along with  the original villagers who inhabited  kakariko  this theory is mainly built upon the  facts that they are in kakariko and they  possess the stone of agony which is  known to be the companion item to the  lens of truth  the former revealing secret grottos by  vibrating the nintendo 64  controller and the latter revealing  hidden areas false walls  and even invisible enemies at the cost  of magic power it is easy to assume the  two objects are related but i don't  necessarily believe this immediately  confirms the family's shika ties  in my opinion their human appearances  disprove any possible ties they might  have  after all the stone could have simply  been stolen by the greedy family  regardless of affiliations  their hair is red and their eyes are  shown to be blue in the 3ds remake of  the game  both features that contrast the  sheikah's iconic white hair and red  eyes their clothing and furniture also  completely lack  any shika symbolism and since their  house is largely in the same condition  as all the other surrounding buildings  plus or minus a few boarded up windows  i think this means that the family moved  into and visibly lived in the house  after kakarika was open to the public  therefore leaving no room for the house  to have been abandoned since the  original chica days  judging from their furniture's design  and their human appearances  they were most likely hylian settlers  that arrived once impa opened the  village to the public  just your average shady filthy rich  family  now as far as how they happen to get  themselves cursed the most obvious  answer is given to us by the old man in  ocarina of time  if you speak to him at night as adult  link inside the house at the bottom of  the stairs  he tells you of a fabulously rich family  in the village that became  cursed due to their greed an obvious  reference to the cursed  sculptura family there is no clear  reason to not believe his words as if  you speak to him while he's walking  around outside in the daytime his  information about the location of the  lens of truth is also correct  the bottom of the well the family's  reputation for riches goes beyond even  the walls of kakariko  if you speak to the zora salesman in the  zora's domain shop he will remark that  the zora armor's fine quality makes it  very expensive  and that only the very rich family of  kakarika village could afford to  purchase it but while it's one thing to  be known for your riches and achieve  fame throughout your successes it's a  completely different situation when you  mix in  the greed factor logically speaking the  only way someone would appear  immorally greedy is if they acted on it  in real life  we would call this stealing in this case  what makes the most sense to me is that  the rich family became  so rich and famous through their acts of  greed or rather  through thievery this doesn't really  matter much but the father of the family  was even  designed to look well kind of sleazy in  my opinion  but either way i think this family of  con artists  being used to making shady deals and  stealing their way to riches  made one deal that they soon came to  regret deeply  the father of the family once his human  form is regained  states that he will try to not get  cursed again meaning the transformations  were obviously not his intent  but rather an accident based on what he  was doing  but to explain this deal i have to jump  from ocarina of time to another  more mature and dark zelda title  twilight princess  in twilight princess there is a very  similar curse made to a very similar  individual in hyrule castle town named  giovanni  this man made a deal for more money and  was turned into money himself  solid gold actually his curse is also a  familiar one  link must find and destroy 100 imp pose  and jovani's curse will be broken  the pattern here is almost completely  identical except for instead of spiders  made out of gold being created because  of the curse  giovanni himself was made into gold two  parties making greedy deals and  receiving a terrifyingly twisted curse  because of it  the curses of the sculptura family and  the curse of giovanni are  so similar to one another that i happen  to believe they may have been created by  the same individual  as do many others however the individual  in question here is where opinions  differ amongst  theorists so what i am going to do in  this video is present to you  three different possibilities for the  one who placed the curses and if you  would  please let me know in the comments below  which one makes the most sense  to you the first possibility would be  taken from the words of a child in  hyrule castle town in twilight princess  who states that giovanni's soul was  taken by the imps  this is a reference to the imp pose that  each must be destroyed to free jovani's  soul  but if the implication here is that he  made his golden deal  with said pose as the zelda pediawiki  also states  this would have to be the same deal  brokered for the sculptura family of  ocarina of time in other words  pose or ghosts are the first possibility  who may have cursed the family after a  deal was made with them  the second possibility is the demon of  hatano village from breath of the wild  trapped within a statue this wicked  individual spends whatever time people  will give him  brokering deals to manipulate the life  forces of his  clients if this individual who calls  himself  a god that governs life and power is  really a demon or other supernatural  being  there's no reason to believe he couldn't  have been alive long long ago in the age  of ocarina of time  he admits that people normally ask him  for riches  and his cynical nature leads me to  believe that he may have promised riches  in gold  to the sculpture family and to jovani  but twisted their fulfillment into the  golden spiders and golden skin  for his own sick amusement the  counter-argument could be made that he  does not make  similar kinds of deals in breath of the  wild but it's clear to me that since  he's been sealed inside of a statue by  hylia herself  he may just be in a weakened state and  unable to perform the same kinds of  curses he used to  i mean i'd imagine that's why highly  asseeled him inside a statue in the  first  place the third and final possibility is  that the deal was made  with an unknown being this sounds like a  strange choice but hear me out  if poe's holding giovanni's curse means  that giovanni made a deal  with a po or pose then logically  speaking  the golden spiders that hold the  sculptural family's curse would mean  that the sculptural family  made a deal with golden spiders or maybe  just  one you see in their house there are  still a few portraits hanging on the far  side of the wall while most of them are  just pictures of creepy individuals or  landscapes  one picture in particular sticks out and  raises some questions  they appear to have a picture of a  golden sculpture hanging on their wall  one that looks slightly different than  the models that appear in game  if they began their transformations  immediately following their golden deal  they wouldn't have been able to hang  these pictures after the curse meaning  for some reason they already knew  about the golden sculptures what if  there is or was  one of these spiders in particular that  they attempted to make a deal with  for more gold like a spider deity of  some sort similar to the golden goose of  fairy tale  there is absolutely no evidence to  support this spider's existence other  than the similar pattern for giovanni  and the picture hanging on the wall but  you have to admit  it's definitely more than odd that it's  there  so which possibility is it was it a poe  a mysterious spider  the demon of hatano village or something  else entirely let me know what you think  in a comment below  also thank you so much for watching the  halloween special this year  and a huge thanks to everyone for  getting the channel to 100  000 subscribers i will be doing  something special to properly celebrate  this milestone so stay tuned for that  coming up  also enormous thanks as always to my  fantastic supporters  of which i have a new face to announce  say hello to merlin  who recently joined the ranks of my  personal heroes if you're interested in  earning my eternal gratitude and helping  the next video come to life  check out that join button below every  video or follow the links in the  description below to find out how  also be sure to drop a like if you  enjoyed this video to get it spread  around on youtube space  and make sure you're subscribed to stick  around for all the nintendo goodness to  come  also down in the description are links  to my social media pages so please feel  free to stop on by and say hi  that's all i've got for this one so i  hope you have a very spooky halloween  this is mass intended bandit signing out  peace  you
 

